"[2511.13182v2] Evaluating Large Language Models for Diacritic Restoration in Romanian Texts: A Comparative Study (https://arxiv.org/abs/2511.13182v2)\nciteturn6311view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 8 months ago; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2511.13182v2\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 202\nL0: cite0†Skip to main content L1: \nL2:  cite53†Image: Cornell University L3: \nL4:  We gratefully acknowledge support from the Simons Foundation, cite1†member institutions†info.arxiv.org , and all contributors. cite2†Donate†info.arxiv.org L5: \nL6: cite54†Image: arxiv logo > cite3†cs > arXiv:2511.13182v2\nL7: \nL8: cite4†Help†info.arxiv.org | cite5†Advanced Search L9: \nL10:  All fields Title Author Abstract Comments Journal reference ACM classification MSC classification Report number arXiv identifier DOI ORCID arXiv author ID Help pages Full text\nL11: \nL12: Search\nL13: cite55†Image: arXiv logo L14: \nL15: cite6† †www.cornell.edu L16: \nL17:  open search\nL18: \nL19: GO\nL20: \nL21: open navigation menu\nL22: ## quick links\nL23: \nL24:   * cite7†Login L25:   * cite4†Help Pages†info.arxiv.org L26:   * cite8†About†info.arxiv.org L27: \nL28: # Computer Science > Computation and Language\nL29: \nL30: arXiv:2511.13182v2 (cs)\nL31: \nL32:  This paper has been withdrawn by Mihai Nadas\nL33: \nL34: [Submitted on 17 Nov 2025 (cite9†v1 ), revised 18 Nov 2025 (this version, v2), latest version 21 Nov 2025 (cite10†v3 )]\nL35: # Title:Evaluating Large Language Models for Diacritic Restoration in Romanian Texts: A Comparative Study\nL36: \nL37: Authors:cite11†Mihai Dan Nadas , cite12†Laura Diosan L38: \nL39: View a PDF of the paper titled Evaluating Large Language Models for Diacritic Restoration in Romanian Texts: A Comparative Study, by Mihai Dan Nadas and 1 other authors\nL40: \nL41: No PDF available, click to view other formats\nL42: > Abstract:Automatic diacritic restoration is crucial for text processing in languages with rich diacritical marks, such as Romanian. This study evaluates the performance of several large language models (LLMs) in restoring diacritics in Romanian texts.\nL43: Using a comprehensive corpus, we tested models including OpenAI's GPT-3.5, GPT-4, GPT-4o, Google's Gemini 1.0 Pro, Meta's Llama 2 and Llama 3, MistralAI's Mixtral 8x7B Instruct, airoboros 70B, and OpenLLM-Ro's RoLlama 2 7B, under multiple prompt templates ranging from zero-shot to complex multi-shot instructions.\nL44: Results show that models such as GPT-4o achieve high diacritic restoration accuracy, consistently surpassing a neutral echo baseline, while others, including Meta's Llama family, exhibit wider variability. These findings highlight the impact of model architecture, training data, and prompt design on diacritic restoration performance and outline promising directions for improving NLP tools for diacritic-rich languages.\nL45: Comments: The original submission contained metadata errors and requires correction. A revised and complete version will be submitted as a replacement\nL46: Subjects: Computation and Language (cs.CL)\nL47: Cite as: cite13†arXiv:2511.13182 [cs.CL]\nL48:   (or  cite14†arXiv:2511.13182v2 [cs.CL] for this version)\nL49:   cite15†https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2511.13182†doi.org L50: \nL51: Focus to learn more\nL52: \nL53:   arXiv-issued DOI via DataCite\nL54: ## Submission history\nL55: \nL56: From: Mihai Nadas [cite16†view email ]\nL57: cite9†[v1] Mon, 17 Nov 2025 09:43:54 UTC (3,433 KB)\nL58: [v2] Tue, 18 Nov 2025 13:16:32 UTC (1 KB) (withdrawn)\nL59: cite10†[v3] Fri, 21 Nov 2025 14:13:16 UTC (2,737 KB)\nL60: \nL61: Full-text links:\nL62: ## Access Paper:\nL63: \nL64:  View a PDF of the paper titled Evaluating Large Language Models for Diacritic Restoration in Romanian Texts: A Comparative Study, by Mihai Dan Nadas and 1 other authors\nL65: \nL66:   * Withdrawn\nL67: \nL68: No license for this version due to withdr